s390/uv: Update PG_arch_1 comment

jira KERNEL-1869
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9
commit-author David Hildenbrand <david@redhat.com>
commit 80cf817949264eff32642aa90da00f03e84e3c0f
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9/80cf8179.failed

We removed the usage of PG_arch_1 for page tables in commit
a51324c430db ("s390/cmma: rework no-dat handling").

Let's update the comment in UV to reflect that.

	Reviewed-by: Claudio Imbrenda <imbrenda@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: David Hildenbrand <david@redhat.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20240508182955.358628-6-david@redhat.com
	Signed-off-by: Heiko Carstens <hca@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Alexander Gordeev <agordeev@linux.ibm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 80cf817949264eff32642aa90da00f03e84e3c0f)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	arch/s390/kernel/uv.c
diff --cc arch/s390/kernel/uv.c
index acbb4ffb87e4,ecfc08902215..000000000000
--- a/arch/s390/kernel/uv.c
+++ b/arch/s390/kernel/uv.c
@@@ -496,20 -495,19 +496,26 @@@ int arch_make_page_accessible(struct pa
  		return 0;
  
  	/*
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	 * PG_arch_1 is used in 3 places:
 +	 * 1. for kernel page tables during early boot
 +	 * 2. for storage keys of huge pages and KVM
 +	 * 3. As an indication that this page might be secure. This can
++=======
+ 	 * PG_arch_1 is used in 2 places:
+ 	 * 1. for storage keys of hugetlb folios and KVM
+ 	 * 2. As an indication that this small folio might be secure. This can
++>>>>>>> 80cf81794926 (s390/uv: Update PG_arch_1 comment)
  	 *    overindicate, e.g. we set the bit before calling
  	 *    convert_to_secure.
- 	 * As secure pages are never huge, all 3 variants can co-exists.
+ 	 * As secure pages are never large folios, both variants can co-exists.
  	 */
 -	if (!test_bit(PG_arch_1, &folio->flags))
 +	if (!test_bit(PG_arch_1, &page->flags))
  		return 0;
  
 -	rc = uv_pin_shared(folio_to_phys(folio));
 +	rc = uv_pin_shared(page_to_phys(page));
  	if (!rc) {
 -		clear_bit(PG_arch_1, &folio->flags);
 +		clear_bit(PG_arch_1, &page->flags);
  		return 0;
  	}
  
* Unmerged path arch/s390/kernel/uv.c
